stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  [*] --> ACTIVE: start, fork, boundary fires, MI child created
  [*] --> WAITING_SCOPE: scope entered (process and saga from M2; subprocess, event subprocess, MI body from S1)
  ACTIVE --> WAITING_USER: userTask
  ACTIVE --> WAITING_ASYNC: async step, TX1
  ACTIVE --> WAITING_TIMER: timer catch
  ACTIVE --> WAITING_EVENT: message, signal or conditional catch, receive task, event-based gateway (S2)
  ACTIVE --> JOINED: parallel, inclusive or complex join, instance row locked
  WAITING_USER --> ACTIVE: task completed
  WAITING_ASYNC --> ACTIVE: TX2 accepts result
  WAITING_TIMER --> ACTIVE: timer fires
  WAITING_EVENT --> ACTIVE: correlated or triggered
  WAITING_USER --> CANCELLED: interrupting boundary, terminate, cancel
  WAITING_ASYNC --> CANCELLED: interrupting boundary, terminate, cancel
  WAITING_TIMER --> CANCELLED: interrupting boundary, terminate, cancel
  WAITING_EVENT --> CANCELLED: other branch of event-based gateway won
  WAITING_SCOPE --> COMPLETED: last child token completed
  WAITING_SCOPE --> CANCELLED: interrupting event subprocess or boundary on the scope
  ACTIVE --> COMPLETED: end event
  COMPLETED --> COMPENSATED: compensation of its activity instances ran
  JOINED --> [*]
  COMPLETED --> [*]
  CANCELLED --> [*]
  COMPENSATED --> [*]
